 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSocket delivery for committed revisions.** WebSockets provide fast updates without a realtime vendor dependency; the project accepts the connection-capacity, session-management, and reconnect work this requires. The change store must support replayable revisions and reliable publication, delivery must manage socket sessions, and browsers must reconnect and catch up after interruption. See [Realtime Board Delivery](decisions/realtime-delivery.md) for the alternatives and trade-off analysis.
